#: ../portal/src/lib/components/docs/SystemRequirements.svelte
msgid "Measured on a production deployment serving 76 sites, then scaled down to a single-site install. The stack is six containers: PostgreSQL, the API, the web frontend, the gateway, the TLS proxy and the updater."
msgstr ""

#: ../portal/src/lib/components/docs/SystemRequirements.svelte
msgid "<0>Memory.</0> Those six use roughly 1 to 1.5 GB between them at rest, most of it PostgreSQL and the API. 2 GB leaves little spare once the operating system is accounted for, which is why it is the floor rather than a comfortable target; the extra memory at 4 GB is used by PostgreSQL as disk cache and is the single cheapest thing you can give it."
msgstr ""

#: ../portal/src/lib/components/docs/SystemRequirements.svelte
msgid "<0>CPU.</0> The API is the only component that does sustained work. One core is enough for a single site, and the whole 76-site deployment above draws about 1.3 cores in total, so headroom here matters less than it looks."
